SCOPE
  Implemented a native SwiftUI + Apple HIG SignalLogViewer page that queries signal
  history from Postgres. The refactored web page composes the shared SignalSelector +
  SignalHistoryTable components; this native page REUSES the existing P3 Apple ports of
  those components (apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/SignalSelector*.swift and
  SignalHistoryTable*.swift) driven through their P1/S8 source seams, and adds the page
  orchestrator + the page-level surfaces (no-vehicle, pre-query idle, error banner).

FILES (allowed scope only)
  + apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry/SignalLogViewerPage.swift        (main View)
  + apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry/SignalLogViewerPageModel.swift   (@Observable model + sources + SI data-source seam)
  + apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry/SignalLogViewerPageViews.swift   (GlassPanel1 controls + idle/no-vehicle/error views + sample source)
  ~ apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings                            (+17 keys: 11 page parity strings + 6 date.preset.* labels; purely additive, 187 insertions/0 deletions)
  ~ apps/parity/apple-ledger.json                                           (rows for page:telemetry/SignalLogViewer)
  ~ .github/prompts/monorepo/logs/apple-page-telemetry-SignalLogViewerPage.log (this log)

ARCHITECTURE (P3 reuse — no re-implementation, no collisions)
  - SignalSelector(model: SignalSelectorModel)  — reused; fed available signals via
    PageBackedSignalSelectorSource from `GET /signals/{vehicleId}/available` (useSignals).
  - SignalHistoryTable(model: SignalHistoryModel) — reused; fed result snapshots via
    PageBackedSignalHistorySource (loading / empty / error / data render branches).
  - Value/format/timestamp/raw-payload use the reused SignalLogInput + SignalValueFormat +
    SignalHistoryFormat helpers (no duplicate SignalLogEntry / SignalHistoryRow / SignalTypeBadge).
  - Units stay SI on the wire; LiveSignalLogDataSource is the KMP-core integration boundary
    (ADR-004), SampleSignalLogDataSource backs previews + the success state.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=17
[x] panel  — GlassPanel1
       SignalLogControlsPanel (SignalLogViewerPageViews.swift) wraps TSGlassPanel and hosts the
       reused SignalSelector + Time Range + Per Page + Query + records-count, mirroring the web
       page's single <GlassPanel className="p-4 sm:p-5 space-y-4"> (GlassPanel1).
[x] state  — loading data state
       SignalLogViewerPageModel.runQuery() sets queryState=.loading and pushes
       SignalHistoryInput(isLoading: true) → SignalHistoryModel.phase == .loading → SHLoadingView
       (skeleton, .redacted). isQuerying drives the Query button ProgressView.
[x] state  — empty data state
       runQuery() sets queryState=.empty when merged rows are empty and pushes empty rows →
       SignalHistoryModel.phase == .empty → SHEmptyView ("No data"). The pre-query idle empty
       (SignalLogIdleView) is rendered while !hasQueried.
[x] state  — error data state
       runQuery() catch sets queryState=.error(message), pushes SignalHistoryInput(errorMessage:)
       → SHErrorView (retry), and the page renders SignalLogErrorBanner at the top (web AlertBanner).
[x] state  — success data state
       runQuery() sets queryState=.success and pushHistorySnapshot() pushes the page slice →
       SignalHistoryModel.phase == .data → SHDataView (Timestamp/Signal/Value/Type + pagination).
[x] string — "Choose one or more signals, set a date range, then hit Query to browse signal history."
       SignalLogIdleView description (SignalLogViewerPageViews.swift). Catalog key present.
[x] string — "Per Page"
       SignalLogControlsPanel.perPageAndQuery field label + Picker. Catalog key present.
[x] string — "Query"
       SignalLogControlsPanel.queryButton label. Catalog key present.
[x] string — "Query signal history from Postgres"
       SignalLogViewerPage.header subtitle. Catalog key present.
[x] string — "Select signals and click Query"
